From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kk: drop the draw of a program that failed to compile, keep the command buffer

A graphics or compute program whose background Metal compile failed set
VK_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER_NV on the command buffer, so vkEndCommandBuffer
returned it. vkd3d-proton only logs that result and submits the command
buffer anyway, which crashed in vkQueueSubmit2 (Exception 0xc0000005 in
Unix call) and hung MSFS 2024 when it started a flight. Drop only the
draw or dispatch, as before, and report it on stderr (first 32 times).

Applies after 0001.
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index af97042..c0bceca 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -3186,7 +3186,17 @@ kk_cmd_shader_pipeline(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_shader *shader,
          /* The pipeline's other program may still be ready */
          struct kk_shader *other = program == shader ? shader->minmax : shader;
          if (other == NULL || !p_atomic_read(&other->pipeline_ready)) {
-            vk_command_buffer_set_error(&cmd->vk, result);
+            /* Only the draw or dispatch is dropped. Failing the command
+             * buffer made vkEndCommandBuffer return the error, and
+             * vkd3d-proton submits such a command buffer anyway, which
+             * crashed in vkQueueSubmit2 and hung MSFS 2024. */
+            static unsigned reported;
+            if (p_atomic_inc_return(&reported) <= 32u)
+               fprintf(stderr, "kk: dropping a %s whose program failed to "
+                               "compile (%d)\n",
+                       shader->vk.stage == MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE ? "dispatch"
+                                                                : "draw",
+                       result);
             return NULL;
          }
          program = other;
